title: Handle relay v3→v2 scheduling rollback for v3-capable parachains

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      If the relay chain rolls back the `CandidateReceiptV3` node feature, a v3-capable parachain
      falls back to producing v2 candidates. The parachain-system runtime now derives "v3 active"
      dynamically from the para constant and the relay feature read from the committed state proof:
      when the feature is off it accepts v2 candidates and keeps the relay-parent-descendant check
      active. The claim-queue-offset bound now depends on that dynamic state: `max_claim_queue_offset()`
      when v3 is active, plus `relay_parent_offset` on the v2 fallback so the fallback lookup is
      accepted and the parachain keeps producing instead of stalling.

crates:
  - name: cumulus-pallet-parachain-system
    bump: minor
